{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014FJEh2drzUGV473FQjeFmZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Plan 26 per-unit path gate (spec sections 8.1, 8.2, 10, 11.3-11.4): N30's wiring.\n2\t\n3\tEvery topology assertion runs against the one real `CompiledStateGraph` that\n4\t`graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph` produces from the real N22/N23 callables,\n5\tand every denominator assertion runs the real node body and the real guard. A\n6\tmock would prove that a stand-in joins correctly, which is the one thing this\n7\tfile exists to rule out.\n8\t\n9\tThe episode now really executes: `_run_episode` streams the one compiled\n10\tproduction graph from D00 to a written terminal, against `RuntimeContext` test\n11\tdoubles and a test-only model transport. Three kinds of test live here:\n12\t\n13\t- assertions about the unit topology that is genuinely registered now,\n14\t- assertions that run one real episode of the real compiled graph, and\n15\t- explicitly named `test_blocked_*` guards that assert the *current, broken*\n16\t  behaviour of a dependency outside this node's write set.\n17\t\n18\tEach blocked guard names its owner and the exact rework that inverts it, and\n19\t`test_every_blocking_gap_is_declared_with_an_owner_and_rework_edge` keeps that\n20\tlist total, so a gap cannot be quietly forgotten once it is fixed: the guard\n21\tfails the moment the rework lands, which is what forces this file to be\n22\trevisited. The guards that closed B-1, B-2 and B-3 were inverted this way and\n23\tnow assert the fixed behaviour instead.\n24\t\n25\tSkips only where the hash-locked environment is absent; the node's evidence was\n26\tproduced by running this file inside it.\n27\t\"\"\"\n28\t\n29\timport ast\n30\timport hashlib\n31\timport inspect\n32\timport json\n33\timport random\n34\timport re\n35\timport sys\n36\timport tempfile\n37\timport unittest\n38\tfrom pathlib import Path\n39\tfrom typing import Any\n40\t\n41\ttry:  # pragma: no 